sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) & Gros et al. (2010) vertebrate limb bud oriented cell division & Wnt5a/FGF8 pushing vs proliferation-gradient hypothesis — MorphoEval overall 89.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py` (overall 89.1/100, down from 93.8/100 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed in reduced form: the St0/St1 limb-bud surfaces are reconstructed as the visual hull of the specimen's two orthogonal OPT iso-surface silhouettes, tetrahedralised (466 nodes / 2150 P1 tets, convergence checked at 1198 nodes), and the paper's 3D Stokes growth system is solved as written with a stabilised P1-P1 FEM verified against two closed-form oracles (8.2e-14) and a Lean-proved volume budget. The parameter-free Model I gives +5.21 % PD (inside the paper's 3.4-11.8 % band) and the FEM 5-regime hierarchy has r = 0.9944 with two fitted gains. The remediation also exposed three defects that lower the score: (i) the Pass 2 \"continuum solver\" credited in v2 is a calibrated 2D boundary-advection model uncoupled from its Poisson field, now disclosed in the docstring and panel titles; (ii) measured proliferation supplies only 12 % of the 66 % OPT volume gain, so the incompressible active-stress Model II fitted to +42.2 % PD must contract AP (-10.9 %) and DV (-14.5 %) while the specimen widens; flank body-wall inflow of 61.4 um/h with no anisotropic stress reproduces PD and the AP/DV signs and gives the best specimen silhouette IoU (0.847 vs 0.770); (iii) the specimen's own St1/St0 PD ratio (1.364) and DV thickness (926 um) disagree with the SHA-locked reference table (1.422; 580 um). Self-test 14/14, 20 measurements, runtime 24 s. Overall 89.1/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/limb_bud_elongation_pushing_comparison.png: rendered output of 2015-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing.py at d58a084, image/png, 1024457 B, 3300×1380 px, artifact_sha256 1b3c6fa5a82c58c70da6b24403feecd75e9d294266957115c8a2488fa8b0e60c (sha256 1b3c6fa5a82c58c70da6b24403feecd75e9d294266957115c8a2488fa8b0e60c), spec_fingerprint 4c3f0cfc301e2c955c4f4f6c7d2e02e3996ca3b4cd571d212368d55baab36b29. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4c3f0cfc301e2c955c4f4f6c7d2e02e3996ca3b4cd571d212368d55baab36b29; artifact_sha256: 1b3c6fa5a82c58c70da6b24403feecd75e9d294266957115c8a2488fa8b0e60c. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Boehm et al. (2010): OPT-measured mouse limb bud growth E11.0 (St0, L_PD 1020 um) -> E11.25 (St1, L_PD 1450 um, +42.2 % PD, +12 % AP, +1 % DV; volume 0.551 -> 0.914 mm^3); dual-label IddU/BrdU cell-cycle atlas (T_c 11-25 h); a 3D Navier-Stokes growth model on a tetrahedral FEM mesh of the OPT iso-surface in which the measured proliferation (Model I) yields only 3.4-11.8 % PD elongation while inverse optimisation demands s_opt > 8 s_emp with negative DV growth; anisotropic/directional growth (Model II) therefore required | Gros et al. (2010): Wnt5a/JNK-controlled oriented cell division and FGF8/MAPK-controlled directional motility drive PD elongation; Wnt5a-/- and FGF-inhibited buds are shorter and more bulbous (E11.5 aspect ratios 2.1 WT, ~1.3 Wnt5a-/-) | Dillon & Othmer (1999): viscous incompressible continuum with distributed sources as the mechanical model of limb-bud outgrowth; Reynolds number irrelevant in the creeping-flow limit; reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3 Section 5: visual-hull reconstruction of the St0/St1 3D surfaces from the vendored specimen's two orthogonal iso-surface silhouettes; conforming prism-split P1 tetrahedral mesh; P1-P1 Brezzi-Pitkaranta-stabilised 3D Stokes growth solver with IddU/BrdU source, extensile oriented-division stress, AER-FGF8 body force, traction-free ectoderm and flank Dirichlet/ALE inflow plane; two closed-form oracles to 8.2e-14; Lagrangian RK2 growth with volume budget closed to 0.5 %; 2-gain calibration (k_chi, k_zeta) with Wnt5a-/-, Model I and uniform control out of sample; flank-influx sweep; mesh-convergence; silhouette IoU against the specimen St1 hull | Pass 2 Sections 2-3 (retained, now labelled): analytic strain-rate laws, IddU/BrdU vs Hooke-Jeeves inverse-opt profiles, a 2D Poisson pressure field used for visualisation, and a 2D boundary-advection model whose per-axis coefficients were calibrated to the 5-regime table; Pass 2 specimen segmentation of 5 sub-panels; transfer_boundary: The 3D geometry is a visual hull of two projections (elliptical cross-sections), not the OPT voxel iso-surface, and the mesh is structured, not unstructured Delaunay; the specimen's own St1/St0 PD ratio (1.364) and DV thickness (926 um) disagree with the reference table (1.422; 580 um) | The 5-regime FEM Pearson r = 0.9944 counts 2 calibrated regimes; the fully out-of-sample set is Model I (+5.2 % vs 10.1 %), Wnt5a-/- (+12.0 % vs 18.5 %) and the uniform control, RMSE 5.3 pp | The Stokes FEM is Reynolds-number independent by construction; the 5-decade Re sweep remains in the 2D reduced model where Re enters only through a phenomenological `re_factor` | Panels C-J of the main figure and 8 of the 20 measurements still come from the calibrated 2D reduced model; does_not_claim: Reproduction of the paper's inverse-optimisation (Hooke-Jeeves) in 3D, chick-embryo (Gros) geometry, cell-level oriented-division statistics, a Navier-Stokes (inertial) solver, or that the active-stress Model II as implemented reproduces the AP/DV changes of the specimen (it does not: AP -10.9 %, DV -14.5 %)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Import the true OPT voxel iso-surface instead of the two-view visual hull (`reconstruct_opt_visual_hull`, L759-800) and replace the structured prism-split mesh (`build_structured_tet_mesh`, L802-868) with an unstructured Delaunay/advancing-front tetrahedralisation; requires vendoring (or re-digitising) OPT volume data as a new SHA-locked dataset file.",
            "remediation needed: Re-verify the SHA-locked reference values that the volume-gap conclusion now rests on — OPT volumes 0.551 -> 0.914 mm^3 and H_DV 580 -> 586 um (`limb_bud_elongation_pushing_reference.json`) — against the specimen (hull H_DV = 926 um, `reconstruct_opt_visual_hull` L759-800) and the paper text; issue a dataset v2 with updated SHA-256 if the table is wrong.",
            "remediation needed: Resolve the AP/DV sign failure of the faithfully solved active-stress Model II (`evaluate_fem_regimes_and_influx`, L1145-1222: WT AP -10.9 %, DV -14.5 % vs OPT +12 %, +1 %): add a DV/AP partition of sigma_active (or a dorsal-ventral ectodermal constraint) and perform a joint fit of (k_zeta, k_chi, v_in) to PD, AP and DV simultaneously instead of PD-only secant calibration (`calibrate_fem_active_rates`, L1109-1143).",
            "remediation needed: Retire or re-couple the Pass 2 2D reduced model (`simulate_limb_bud_regime`, L336-506): its per-axis coefficients are fitted, it is uncoupled from `solve_continuum_pressure_velocity_field` (L244-334), and its `re_factor` (L270-273) is the only source of the 'Reynolds insensitivity' measurement; Panels C-J and 8 of 20 measurements should be moved onto the FEM or explicitly demoted.",
            "remediation needed: Wnt5a-/- is under-predicted out of sample (11.97 % vs 18.5 %, `measure_morphoeval` L1873-1881): test whether the Wnt5a(x) weighting w(x) in `simulate_limb_bud_fem_3d` (L989-1095) or the residual FGF8 gain in the mutant (chi = 0.25) is responsible, using the Gros et al. (2010) E11.5 aspect-ratio data as a second constraint." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.891"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 017 Pass 2 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

